\section*{Weak inhomogeneous Duffin-Schaeffer}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 022; 2026-09-25), the asserted result is that divergence of the totient-weighted approximation sum implies infinitely many inhomogeneous approximations for almost every real number, for every fixed shift and without reduced-numerator conditions.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 022; 2026-09-25), close interval pairs are measured through determinant coordinates and weighted least common multiples. Exact rational coincidences are charged separately, while arithmetic extraction and a density purge give summable savings for the remaining shifted overlaps.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The result supplies the conclusion in this problem with its displayed hypotheses and quantifiers. The broader statements and applications in the manuscript are kept separate from the particular question above. The supporting result is manuscript 1 (family 022; 2026-09-25).

